Since your request didn't say what the code should do, here's a working Java program that matches the tool I have: it **deletes log files older than a set number of days**. It has the same options as the tool: a folder path, an age limit, a file extension, recursive search and a dry-run mode.

### LogCleanup.java

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.nio.file.attribute.BasicFileAttributes;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class LogCleanup {

    /**
     * Deletes log files older than the given number of days.
     *
     * @param directory     the folder to search
     * @param ageLimitDays  files older than this many days are deleted
     * @param extension     file extension without the dot (e.g. "log")
     * @param recursive     whether to search subfolders too
     * @param simulate      if true, only list the files without deleting them
     * @return the number of files deleted (or that would be deleted)
     */
    public static int cleanupLogs(Path directory, int ageLimitDays, String extension,
                                  boolean recursive, boolean simulate) throws IOException {

        if (!Files.isDirectory(directory)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Not a directory: " + directory);
        }

        Instant cutoff = Instant.now().minus(ageLimitDays, ChronoUnit.DAYS);
        String suffix = "." + extension.toLowerCase();
        int maxDepth = recursive ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : 1;
        int count = 0;

        try (Stream<Path> paths = Files.walk(directory, maxDepth)) {
            for (Path file : (Iterable<Path>) paths::iterator) {
                if (!Files.isRegularFile(file)) continue;
                if (!file.getFileName().toString().toLowerCase().endsWith(suffix)) continue;

                BasicFileAttributes attrs = Files.readAttributes(file, BasicFileAttributes.class);
                Instant lastModified = attrs.lastModifiedTime().toInstant();

                if (lastModified.isBefore(cutoff)) {
                    if (simulate) {
                        System.out.println("[DRY RUN] Would delete: " + file);
                    } else {
                        try {
                            Files.delete(file);
                            System.out.println("Deleted: " + file);
                        } catch (IOException e) {
                            System.err.println("Failed to delete " + file + ": " + e.getMessage());
                            continue;
                        }
                    }
                    count++;
                }
            }
        }
        return count;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        if (args.length < 2) {
            System.out.println("Usage: java LogCleanup <path> <ageLimitDays> [extension] [recursive] [simulate]");
            System.out.println("Example: java LogCleanup /var/log/myapp 30 log true true");
            return;
        }

        Path path = Paths.get(args[0]);
        int ageLimit = Integer.parseInt(args[1]);
        String extension = args.length > 2 ? args[2] : "log";
        boolean recursive = args.length > 3 && Boolean.parseBoolean(args[3]);
        boolean simulate = args.length > 4 && Boolean.parseBoolean(args[4]);

        try {
            int result = cleanupLogs(path, ageLimit, extension, recursive, simulate);
            System.out.println((simulate ? "Files that would be deleted: " : "Files deleted: ") + result);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

### How to run it

```bash
javac LogCleanup.java
java LogCleanup /var/log/myapp 30 log true true   # dry run: list .log files older than 30 days, including subfolders
java LogCleanup /var/log/myapp 30                 # actually delete .log files older than 30 days
```

